2026-11-06T03:20:05.1503271Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1513808Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1514733Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1515463Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1515823Z 
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1516096Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1516824Z 
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1517165Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1517909Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1518306Z 
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1518532Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1519005Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1519367Z 
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1519676Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1520316Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:20:05.1520571Z 
